{"signature": "6ed2c06db4ec59ad723a35244c8ad7939339cea1394d7e611e7752065b0d3468", "result": {"checks": {"check": {"scope": {"id": "check", "service": "confluence", "file": "confluence_working.json", "pointer": "/pages", "field": "author_id", "values": ["user_EMPLOYEE_0005"]}, "matches": [{"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/confluence/confluence_working.json", "pointer": "/pages/18", "field": "author_id", "value": "user_EMPLOYEE_0005", "record": {"id": "page_economy_design", "space_id": "space_PROD", "parent_id": "page_prod_home", "title": "Economy Design \u2014 Coins, Lives & Boosters", "body": "<p>This page is the cross-game reference for how our soft and hard currencies, lives, and boosters are priced and tuned. It is owned by Design and kept in sync with the individual game design docs - see <ac:link><ri:page ri:content-title=\"Domino Delights \u2014 Game Design Document\"/><ac:link-body>Domino Delights - Game Design Document</ac:link-body></ac:link> and <ac:link><ri:page ri:content-title=\"Zombie Match 3D \u2014 Game Design Document\"/><ac:link-body>Zombie Match 3D - Game Design Document</ac:link-body></ac:link> for the per-game economy layers built on top of these primitives.</p><h2>Currency model</h2><p>The currency model is per title. Zombie Match 3D uses coins, gems and bones; Domino Delights uses coins, gems and hero shards; Combo Fighter uses Silver, Gold, Experience, Gems and Tickets. Gems is the only currency common to all three by name; Combo Fighter's soft currencies are Silver and Gold rather than coins, so the shared primitive is the soft/hard pair, not the word \"coins\". Coins are the soft currency earned in play; gems are the premium hard currency bought or awarded sparingly. The conversion below is the Zombie Match 3D reference; Domino Delights adjusted its IAP payouts the same month (commit <code>ceb6021fb</code>, 9 April 2025):</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Unit</th><th>Equals</th><th>Notes</th></tr><tr><td>1 US dollar</td><td>1,000 coins</td><td>Reference peg for IAP sizing; not a direct store SKU.</td></tr><tr><td>1 gem</td><td>10 coins</td><td>Hard currency; used for premium sinks and gating.</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Level victories pay out coins on a per-level band, which anchors the earn side of the loop against the booster sinks below.</p><h3>Zombie Match 3D item catalog</h3><p>The ZM3D Master Item List is the source of truth for tunable objects: it currently holds <strong>250</strong> items spread across 21 categories (boosters, tiles, cosmetics, packs, and event-only entitlements). When adding a category, register it here first so the balancing sheet and the client stay aligned.</p><h2>Booster costs</h2><p>Currency units and values are title-specific; only the general soft-/hard-currency pattern is shared. The retained source confirms these Zombie Match 3D per-unit coin values and does not support a 1,500-coin, 30-minute unlimited assignment.</p><h3>Zombie Match 3D</h3><table><tbody><tr><th>Booster</th><th>Per-unit coin cost</th></tr><tr><td>Broom</td><td>10 Gems</td></tr><tr><td>Tornado</td><td>12 Gems</td></tr><tr><td>Catapult</td><td>15 Gems</td></tr><tr><td>Taser</td><td>20 Gems</td></tr><tr><td>Glue (pre-level, one use)</td><td>400 Coins</td></tr><tr><td>Trampoline (pre-level, one use)</td><td>200 Coins</td></tr><tr><td>Trampoline or Glue, rotating shop (30 minutes unlimited)</td><td>1,500 Coins</td></tr></tbody></table><h3>Domino Delights</h3><table><tbody><tr><th>Booster</th><th>Cost</th><th>Currency</th></tr><tr><td>Rewind</td><td>500</td><td>Coins</td></tr><tr><td>Dynamite</td><td>1,000</td><td>Coins</td></tr><tr><td>Draw 3</td><td>1,200</td><td>Coins</td></tr><tr><td>Wildcard</td><td>1,600</td><td>Coins</td></tr><tr><td>Draw 5 (out-of-moves continue only)</td><td>1,800</td><td>Coins</td></tr><tr><td>Gust</td><td>2,000</td><td>Coins</td></tr></tbody></table><ul><li>Domino Delights' main shop prices in coins on a much wider ladder; see <ac:link><ri:page ri:content-title=\"Domino Delights &mdash; Game Design Document\"/><ac:link-body>Domino Delights - Game Design Document</ac:link-body></ac:link> for the per-level earn curve these sit against.</li><li>The daily rotating shop carries gem-priced equivalents of the same boosters &mdash; Rewind 50, Dynamite 100, Draw 3 120, Wildcard 160, Gust 200 Gems &mdash; so the shop is not coin-only even though every in-level charge above is. Draw 5 has no shop SKU at all; 1,800 Coins is strictly the out-of-moves continue price.</li><li>The two games do <strong>not</strong> share a booster price band - only the currency model is shared.</li></ul><h2>The Domino Delights coin cut (April 2025)</h2><ac:structured-macro ac:name=\"warning\"><ac:rich-text-body><p>In <strong>April 2025</strong> we cut Domino Delights <em>first-time level-completion</em> coin rewards by 34.4% - the nine-cell star table fell from a 480-coin sum to 315 - to stop runaway coin inflation. A straight 50% cut was the preferred option on paper, but it is not what shipped. The star table was not the only faucet cut in the same window &mdash; on-board chest coins went 300 to 100, hourly collection 150 to 100, chapter rewards 1000 to 500, the 4-streak multiplier 80x to 40x, mini-game refresh 2h to 24h, and Lucky Drop's infinite-lives grant 1800s to 300s &mdash; which is why the p99 falls further than the star-table percentage alone would suggest. The 99th-percentile daily earn fell from about 25,000 coins to about 8,500. IAP payouts were re-tuned the same month (commit <code>ceb6021fb</code>, 9 April 2025); the size of that offset was never written down, so do not quote one. Do not revert reward payouts on GoD without re-running the sink analysis - the pre-cut curve is recoverable from commit <code>1ee438b6a6</code> and from the v2.0 economy workbook.</p></ac:rich-text-body></ac:structured-macro><p>The symptom was that high-engagement players accumulated coins faster than any sink could absorb, so boosters felt free and the difficulty curve flattened. After the cut, average booster spend nudged up as expected and the coin balance distribution stopped climbing. The changes were applied to the live economy tables under the \"Game of Dominoes\" (GoD) codename and mirrored into this page's tuning constants.</p><ac:structured-macro ac:name=\"info\"><ac:rich-text-body><p>Lives regeneration and refill pricing are game-specific and documented in each GDD. This page only fixes the shared currency and booster primitives.</p></ac:rich-text-body></ac:structured-macro>", "body_format": "storage", "status": "current", "version": 3, "author_id": "user_EMPLOYEE_0005", "created_at": "2024-06-01T18:11:38Z", "updated_at": "2025-09-21T02:19:30Z"}}], "records_checked": 31, "files_selected": 1, "files_completed": 1, "scan_complete": true, "errors": []}}, "files_read_this_call": 1, "sources": [{"file": "HarmonyGames_Other_Services/Services_Data/confluence/confluence_working.json", "manifest_sha256": "e6840608051cf49e37aeb94a719fed78e0d38eb902d30f86805b84ea0d67adb6", "freshness": "970c4a92af37d08dd66b69b75daa8db99f043a7078d21e855c130a5f6081383c"}], "scan_complete": true, "persona_filtered": false, "backend": "grouped-record-scan", "scope_note": "Exact direct fields in selected arrays. No SQL is applied. Absence/uniqueness is supported only within complete declared scopes. Manifest hashes are declared provenance, not fresh full-content hashes."}, "checksum": "7caf147af92fb7e9d1e22154af908be578a85a4f804a0cd0c1fe80be76c5c432"}